{
  "title": "豐盛不是金幣",
  "title_en": "Abundance Cannot Be Kept",
  "series": "神話未完成",
  "series_en": "Myths in the Making",
  "volume": 10,
  "model": "史旺姬",
  "creator": "史旺基 Swanky",
  "slug": "swanky-ji-abundance-without-coins",
  "date": "2026-10-22",
  "count": 36,
  "cover_photo": 17,
  "setting": "黑米築牆的夜間倉場",
  "subtitle": "讓牆重新成為一把米。",
  "subtitle_en": "Let the wall become a handful of grain again.",
  "lead": "吉祥天走進由糧食築成的房間。穀粒緊密地站立，成為牆、圓筒與高座；每一道完整的輪廓，都讓一把米變得難以取走。她逐一鬆開金屬箍，讓向下的重量重新屬於穀粒。有人拿來杯子，有人推來托盤，也有人從最低的一圈開始。豐盛在這裡發生於物件改變形狀、人的手終於可以參與的時刻。",
  "lead_en": "Lakshmi enters rooms built from food. Packed grain stands as walls, cylinders and a raised seat; each unbroken outline makes a handful harder to take. She loosens the metal bands, returning the grain to its downward weight. Someone brings a cup, someone pushes a tray, and someone begins at the lowest ring. Abundance happens as objects change shape and other hands find a way in.",
  "statement": "吉祥天走進由糧食築成的房間。穀粒緊密地站立，成為牆、圓筒與高座；每一道完整的輪廓，都讓一把米變得難以取走。她逐一鬆開金屬箍，讓向下的重量重新屬於穀粒。有人拿來杯子，有人推來托盤，也有人從最低的一圈開始。豐盛在這裡發生於物件改變形狀、人的手終於可以參與的時刻。\n\n最後要鬆開的，是她自己的座位。當包圍木板的穀粒落下，座位仍由鋼腳支撐，卻不再需要一圈糧食替它劃出位置。人們可以帶走需要的部分，也可以留下空杯。她退回通路的一側，讓彼此的相遇不再以保管與索取開始。",
  "statement_en": "Lakshmi enters rooms built from food. Packed grain stands as walls, cylinders and a raised seat; each unbroken outline makes a handful harder to take. She loosens the metal bands, returning the grain to its downward weight. Someone brings a cup, someone pushes a tray, and someone begins at the lowest ring. Abundance happens as objects change shape and other hands find a way in.\n\nThe last band surrounds her own seat. As its grain falls away, steel legs still support the wood, but food no longer has to mark out her place. People can carry away what they need or leave an empty cup. She steps to one side of the passage, allowing an encounter to begin without custody or a claim.",
  "afterword": "最後要鬆開的，是她自己的座位。當包圍木板的穀粒落下，座位仍由鋼腳支撐，卻不再需要一圈糧食替它劃出位置。人們可以帶走需要的部分，也可以留下空杯。她退回通路的一側，讓彼此的相遇不再以保管與索取開始。",
  "afterword_en": "The last band surrounds her own seat. As its grain falls away, steel legs still support the wood, but food no longer has to mark out her place. People can carry away what they need or leave an empty cup. She steps to one side of the passage, allowing an encounter to begin without custody or a claim.",
  "series_statement": "《神話未完成》\n史旺姬走進流傳至今的神話，留下它最核心的問題，讓它面對今天的生活。神話一直被講述、被使用，所以還沒有完成。",
  "series_statement_en": "Myths in the Making\nSwanky Ji steps into myths that are still being told, keeps the question at their heart, and lets it meet the life we live now. A myth that is still told and still used is not yet finished.",
  "story_zh": "《Sri Sukta》對吉祥的召喚包含財富、食物與滋養；吉祥天的圖像傳統也以蓮花、金色與豐饒相連。本冊從這份豐盛出發，把黑米、金屬箍與夜間工作場域組成一連串開放的動作：一種曾被維持的形狀，逐漸成為可以使用、也可以離開的事物。",
  "story_en": "The Sri Sukta invokes prosperity through wealth, food and nourishment; Lakshmi’s visual tradition also connects her with the lotus, gold and plenty. This book begins with that abundance, arranging black rice, metal bands and workplaces at night into a sequence of openings. A carefully maintained form gradually becomes something people can use, and something they are free to leave.",
  "sources_zh": "故事參考：Sri Sukta — Swami Krishnananda（https://www.swami-krishnananda.org/invoc/in_sria.html）；Lakshmi, 1894 — The Metropolitan Museum of Art（https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/78264）",
  "sources_en": "Story references: Sri Sukta — Swami Krishnananda (https://www.swami-krishnananda.org/invoc/in_sria.html); Lakshmi, 1894 — The Metropolitan Museum of Art (https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/78264)",
  "credit": "創作與攝影概念：史旺基 · 角色：史旺姬",
  "credit_en": "Creative direction and photographic concept: Swanky · Character: Swanky Ji",
